    "bio": "a Representative from North Carolina; born in Surry County, N.C., in 1772; member of the North Carolina state house of commons in 1800 and 1801; served in the North Carolina state senate in 1828, 1829, and 1838; elected as a Democratic Republican to the Tenth and to the three succeeding Congresses (March 4, 1807-March 3, 1815); died in Surry County, N.C., December 18, 1839; interment on his estate in Surry County, N.C. (now known as the Edwards-Franklin House).",
